  "body": "MAINLINE-034 complete, QUESTIONABLE/PROJECTION. For the inherited 24-hour mission, select ground evacuation then sealed service at an estimated 30–50 kg onboard for both leads; retain the existing 100 kg allowance. Assembly gas-load measurement and evacuation of every cell/bore remain conditions.\n\nConditioned source-rate hot-pressure limits are 398.2/7.76/19.49 days for P2/Kapton P3/Zylon-barrier P3. Times to 48.894 kg free gas are 464.9/13.97/35.83 days. These are conditional gas calculations, not qualified endurance; the assumed power package supports at most nine days of 5 W monitoring.\n\nBoth P3 frames are SiC; CFRP denotes end wraps. Unvented ambient air would retain 43.4/88.2/76.1 kg. Outgassing changes phase of existing onboard mass; external ingress adds mass, and getters retain it. Water beds and powered pumps are explicitly sized; the continuous P3 benchmark is 292.3 kg and its Kapton speed is 2.3% short under assumed conductance.\n\nZylon vacuum equipment plus barrier/attachment and fitting adhesive totals 91.6–111.6 kg; no payload credit. Kapton structural SF remains below one.\n\n36 numerical/source checks pass; 53 upstream/prior pins unchanged. The manifest pins 77 files, including sources, calculator, curves and delivery checks. Seventeen nonblocking physical/source NFIs remain. No upstream code inspected, imported or run. Stop-and-file instruction fulfilled; no successor named.",
